Revisit Leetcode 904. fruits into baskets , same as logic of solution 1

Intuition :
The only two difference of both the question are :
array of number with limit 2 and characters with limit k


Logic :

Initialise map for storing frequency of each character
while size of map exceeds 2 , then move left pointer , and reduce its frequency in map
and , if the character in the map equals zero , which tells that the cjharacter if not in the window , hence remove that key
and , increment left pointer
add the element in map if it not present , otherwise , increase its frequency
if the size of map less than or equal to 2 , then calculate the window length


Code :

public static int Longestsubstring(String str, int k) {
    HashMap<Character, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
    int left = 0;
    int maxlen = 0;
    for (int right = 0; right < str.length(); right++) {
        map.put(str.charAt(right), map.getOrDefault(str.charAt(right), 0) + 1);
        while (map.size() > k) {
            char ch = str.charAt(left);
            map.put(ch, map.get(ch) - 1);
            if (map.get(ch) == 0) {
                map.remove(ch);
            }
            left++;
        }
        maxlen = Math.max(maxlen, right - left + 1);
    }
    return maxlen;
}
